1
00:00:01,376 --> 00:00:03,420
♪

2
00:00:04,296 --> 00:00:06,256
[energy snapping]

3
00:00:07,549 --> 00:00:10,677
[Asta yelling]

4
00:00:26,068 --> 00:00:28,237
[grunts] Huh.

5
00:00:32,824 --> 00:00:34,534
Just two minutes left.

6
00:00:34,618 --> 00:00:35,702
My second sword.

7
00:00:37,412 --> 00:00:38,830
Demon-Dweller!

8
00:00:39,581 --> 00:00:41,208
[slashing]

9
00:00:52,844 --> 00:00:54,721
Destroyer!

10
00:00:57,307 --> 00:00:59,726
[LILITH]
What sort of creature is this?

11
00:01:01,812 --> 00:01:03,855
[LIEBE]
I was the weakest of the weak

12
00:01:03,939 --> 00:01:05,399
back in the underworld.

13
00:01:05,482 --> 00:01:09,111
I never would've stood a chance
against supreme devils.

14
00:01:10,153 --> 00:01:13,240
Please, Liebe. Live... okay?

15
00:01:14,575 --> 00:01:17,202
I love you, my sweet little boy.

16
00:01:17,286 --> 00:01:19,121
[ASTA] The reason I've been able
to fight up until now

17
00:01:19,204 --> 00:01:20,497
is all thanks to you,

18
00:01:20,581 --> 00:01:23,041
so, seriously,
thank you so much!

19
00:01:24,084 --> 00:01:26,962
[Liebe giggles]
That's my line, dumb-ass!

20
00:01:27,045 --> 00:01:30,507
Thanks to you,
I get to fight these guys!

21
00:01:30,591 --> 00:01:33,885
-[LILITH] No. It's impossible.
-[Asta grunts]

22
00:01:33,969 --> 00:01:35,679
[LILITH] There shouldn't be
a creature alive

23
00:01:35,762 --> 00:01:38,557
that can attack me or withstand
my attack for this long!

24
00:01:38,640 --> 00:01:40,100
[shatters]

25
00:01:40,183 --> 00:01:43,770
Humans, weaker devils,
they're all mere playthings

26
00:01:43,854 --> 00:01:45,480
meant to entertain me.

27
00:01:45,564 --> 00:01:46,440
What?

28
00:01:46,523 --> 00:01:48,108
♪

29
00:01:49,067 --> 00:01:51,612
I'm not having fun anymore.

30
00:01:52,279 --> 00:01:53,905
What the hell are you?!

31
00:01:55,949 --> 00:01:57,409
[shudders]

32
00:01:57,492 --> 00:02:00,370
And what is this
horrible feeling?!

33
00:02:00,454 --> 00:02:02,164
It's a new one for your kind.

34
00:02:02,247 --> 00:02:04,374
Never had to identify it before.

35
00:02:04,458 --> 00:02:07,002
After all, you're the big bads

36
00:02:07,085 --> 00:02:09,504
ruling over the first level
of the underworld,

37
00:02:09,588 --> 00:02:11,882
so there was nothing
that could threaten you.

38
00:02:11,965 --> 00:02:14,176
So of course you wouldn't know!

39
00:02:14,259 --> 00:02:16,595
But that feeling's called fear!

40
00:02:16,678 --> 00:02:17,637
[gasps]

41
00:02:21,099 --> 00:02:22,517
[gasps, exclaims]

42
00:02:23,185 --> 00:02:25,103
Hey, come back here, you jerk!

43
00:02:25,729 --> 00:02:27,898
[LILITH] It appears that
he can only maintain that form

44
00:02:27,981 --> 00:02:29,316
for a limited time.

45
00:02:30,150 --> 00:02:32,486
If I retreat for now,
I can still win.

46
00:02:33,111 --> 00:02:34,279
Oh, man, they're fast.

47
00:02:34,988 --> 00:02:36,656
Too fast. I can't catch up.

48
00:02:37,324 --> 00:02:38,742
[Lilith chuckles slyly]

49
00:02:39,743 --> 00:02:42,871
Don't worry, I'll tear you
limb from limb soon enough!

50
00:02:42,954 --> 00:02:44,289
Your little friends, too,

51
00:02:44,373 --> 00:02:47,167
and all the humans
in this world!

52
00:02:48,001 --> 00:02:48,877
[NACHT] Think again!

53
00:02:50,253 --> 00:02:51,213
I can't beat you,

54
00:02:51,296 --> 00:02:52,881
but I can hold you
while he does.

55
00:02:53,924 --> 00:02:55,926
-[whimpering]
-[NACHT] Ironic, isn't it?

56
00:02:56,009 --> 00:02:58,261
You have an unfathomable
amount of mana,

57
00:02:58,345 --> 00:02:59,805
and these are the ones you fear!

58
00:02:59,888 --> 00:03:01,848
[yelling]

59
00:03:01,932 --> 00:03:04,559
[battle cry]

60
00:03:06,561 --> 00:03:08,355
Keep your hands off...

61
00:03:08,438 --> 00:03:09,314
[gasps]

62
00:03:09,398 --> 00:03:12,442
...this world!

63
00:03:16,988 --> 00:03:19,449
[Lilith exclaiming in disbelief]

64
00:03:19,533 --> 00:03:20,909
[grunts softly]

65
00:03:21,910 --> 00:03:22,911
Hmm.

66
00:03:23,703 --> 00:03:26,123
A human and devil with no magic.

67
00:03:29,793 --> 00:03:31,711
[exclaims happily, chuckles]

68
00:03:31,795 --> 00:03:33,380
Huh?

69
00:03:35,215 --> 00:03:36,508
[both grunt, chuckle]

70
00:03:55,610 --> 00:03:56,945
[NACHT] You've improved,

71
00:03:57,612 --> 00:04:00,532
but it's clear you haven't
fully mastered Devil Union yet.

72
00:04:01,283 --> 00:04:03,410
Still, well done, you idiot.

73
00:04:04,035 --> 00:04:05,454
Uh...

74
00:04:05,537 --> 00:04:07,747
[chuckles] That's something
Captain Yami would say.

75
00:04:07,831 --> 00:04:10,333
-You two are a lot alike.
-Hmm.

76
00:04:11,001 --> 00:04:12,502
-[shrieking]
-I would strongly advise

77
00:04:12,586 --> 00:04:13,920
taking that back.

78
00:04:14,004 --> 00:04:16,465
I don't get it. What did I do?

79
00:04:16,548 --> 00:04:17,632
[grunting]

80
00:04:19,050 --> 00:04:20,635
[NACHT] Whenever I see him,

81
00:04:20,719 --> 00:04:22,762
I'm reminded of the person
I used to be.

82
00:04:24,347 --> 00:04:25,849
[ASTA]
Ow! Ow, ow, ow, ow, ow, ow!

83
00:04:25,932 --> 00:04:26,975
Not again!

84
00:04:27,350 --> 00:04:30,187
My whole body hurts like crazy
after Devil Union,

85
00:04:30,270 --> 00:04:32,063
and I won't be able to use it
or my dark mode

86
00:04:32,147 --> 00:04:33,732
for half an hour!

87
00:04:33,815 --> 00:04:34,983
-[grunts]
-[Asta crying dramatically]

88
00:04:35,066 --> 00:04:37,027
-It hurts so much!
-Half an hour, huh?

89
00:04:37,694 --> 00:04:39,404
The Dark Triad is wielding power

90
00:04:39,488 --> 00:04:42,240
nearly equal to that
of the supreme devils.

91
00:04:42,324 --> 00:04:44,993
Withstanding it for 30 minutes
will be tough.

92
00:04:45,994 --> 00:04:48,997
Morris opening the underworld
gates faster is also a problem.

93
00:04:49,956 --> 00:04:50,874
But at the moment,

94
00:04:51,291 --> 00:04:53,502
our top priority
is to take down the Dark Triad

95
00:04:53,585 --> 00:04:55,003
as quickly as possible.

96
00:04:55,086 --> 00:04:56,171
[exclaiming in agony]

97
00:04:56,254 --> 00:04:57,714
[NACHT]
Even without Devil Union,

98
00:04:57,798 --> 00:04:59,508
his anti-magic
should prove useful.

99
00:05:00,383 --> 00:05:01,301
[Asta yelping]

100
00:05:01,384 --> 00:05:02,761
[NACHT] Three battles,

101
00:05:02,844 --> 00:05:04,930
one more dire than the others.

102
00:05:05,013 --> 00:05:07,265
-[wind whistling]
-[heavy slashes]

103
00:05:09,476 --> 00:05:11,770
♪

104
00:05:14,606 --> 00:05:15,857
[grunts]

105
00:05:18,485 --> 00:05:21,196
It appears that the properties
of your magic can change,

106
00:05:21,279 --> 00:05:23,865
adjusting as needed
to your opponent's abilities.

107
00:05:24,491 --> 00:05:25,617
At this level, however,

108
00:05:25,951 --> 00:05:28,495
my body magic is more than
a match for even that.

109
00:05:29,955 --> 00:05:33,083
Lasting as long as you did
was quite a feat,

110
00:05:33,166 --> 00:05:34,876
-but you're at your limit.
-[Jack heaving]

111
00:05:35,544 --> 00:05:37,128
You've got a big, dumb mouth.

112
00:05:37,212 --> 00:05:40,215
I could fix that
by slicing it off your face!

113
00:05:41,258 --> 00:05:43,635
As thanks
for being so entertaining,

114
00:05:43,718 --> 00:05:46,179
I'll make yours
a spectacular death.

115
00:05:46,263 --> 00:05:47,389
[grunts]

116
00:05:50,183 --> 00:05:52,811
-[MAGNA] Exploding Fireball!
-[DANTE] Hmm.

117
00:05:54,646 --> 00:05:56,648
[footsteps approaching]

118
00:05:58,650 --> 00:06:01,069
[grunts] Huh?

119
00:06:12,205 --> 00:06:14,708
What's up? How's it going?

120
00:06:15,667 --> 00:06:16,543
Huh?

121
00:06:17,335 --> 00:06:19,212
Who are these strange people?

122
00:06:21,715 --> 00:06:23,466
A couple of peons.

123
00:06:23,550 --> 00:06:27,220
This is no place for weaklings
such as yourselves.

124
00:06:27,887 --> 00:06:30,599
[JACK] Yami's peasants?
Where did they come from?

125
00:06:30,682 --> 00:06:32,934
What the hell
do you think you're doing here?

126
00:06:33,018 --> 00:06:34,811
You two got a death wish?

127
00:06:34,894 --> 00:06:35,854
[DANTE] Good question.

128
00:06:36,271 --> 00:06:37,606
I don't know what you think
you'll accomplish.

129
00:06:37,981 --> 00:06:39,816
[MAGNA] Yeah, yeah, we came to
kick your devil-possessed asses

130
00:06:39,899 --> 00:06:41,610
and save Captain Yami.

131
00:06:41,693 --> 00:06:43,987
There are those
who still make amusing opponents

132
00:06:44,070 --> 00:06:46,406
despite being less powerful
than I am.

133
00:06:46,489 --> 00:06:48,575
Like him, for example.

134
00:06:48,658 --> 00:06:52,162
But you,
your mana is far too low.

135
00:06:52,245 --> 00:06:53,371
[wind howling]

136
00:06:53,455 --> 00:06:55,582
You're nothing.
Not anti-magic users,

137
00:06:55,665 --> 00:06:58,168
no arcane stage mages
with unique powers.

138
00:06:58,251 --> 00:06:59,210
Even with both of you

139
00:06:59,294 --> 00:07:00,253
-attacking at once--
-Oh, you got

140
00:07:00,337 --> 00:07:01,421
the wrong idea, pal.

141
00:07:01,504 --> 00:07:02,464
[Zora cackles]

142
00:07:03,131 --> 00:07:05,258
I'll be taking you down
all by myself.

143
00:07:05,342 --> 00:07:07,719
Huh? [chuckles]

144
00:07:10,930 --> 00:07:14,017
[laughing scornfully]

145
00:07:14,684 --> 00:07:17,896
You mock me
with your pathetic bravado!

146
00:07:18,521 --> 00:07:19,856
[MAGNA] So strong.

147
00:07:19,940 --> 00:07:20,982
[DANTE] A "fight" between us

148
00:07:21,066 --> 00:07:23,068
wouldn't even be worthy
of the name.

149
00:07:24,361 --> 00:07:25,570
[MAGNA] I'm not an idiot.

150
00:07:26,279 --> 00:07:28,156
I know you're crazy powerful.

151
00:07:28,865 --> 00:07:30,158
♪

152
00:07:30,784 --> 00:07:33,536
[yelling] Captain Yami!

153
00:07:34,204 --> 00:07:35,789
That spell's not ready
to use yet.

154
00:07:36,539 --> 00:07:39,125
If you go out there now,
you won't be any use.

155
00:07:39,209 --> 00:07:41,795
You'll either get in the way
or die!

156
00:07:42,671 --> 00:07:44,297
[Magna grunting]

157
00:07:51,763 --> 00:07:53,807
And I know that I'm weak.

158
00:07:54,516 --> 00:07:56,559
I've known it for a long time.

159
00:07:56,643 --> 00:07:57,811
[stifled sobbing]

160
00:08:00,897 --> 00:08:02,816
But I can't go
crawling back to them

161
00:08:02,899 --> 00:08:04,150
no better than I was before

162
00:08:04,234 --> 00:08:06,236
and pretend like
it's no big deal.

163
00:08:06,945 --> 00:08:08,071
[wind howling]

164
00:08:08,154 --> 00:08:10,573
I have no intention
of sullying my magic

165
00:08:10,657 --> 00:08:13,118
by using it against
a piece of garbage like you.

166
00:08:13,743 --> 00:08:15,662
Attack me
to your heart's content,

167
00:08:16,287 --> 00:08:20,083
and once you're satisfied,
take your friend and leave.

168
00:08:20,166 --> 00:08:21,584
If that's what you want,

169
00:08:21,668 --> 00:08:23,962
then don't mind if I do!

170
00:08:25,630 --> 00:08:26,798
[explosion]

171
00:08:26,881 --> 00:08:28,800
There's no point! [grunts]

172
00:08:29,843 --> 00:08:32,053
Well? Are you finished?

173
00:08:32,137 --> 00:08:33,555
[wind howling]

174
00:08:34,639 --> 00:08:36,349
-[Magna grunts]
-Huh?

175
00:08:36,433 --> 00:08:37,559
[chain rattling]

176
00:08:37,642 --> 00:08:39,894
♪

177
00:08:39,978 --> 00:08:41,062
[DANTE] A chain?

178
00:08:42,105 --> 00:08:43,273
What is this?

179
00:08:47,569 --> 00:08:49,195
[chain rattling]

180
00:08:51,489 --> 00:08:52,949
[metal clanging]

181
00:08:54,325 --> 00:08:56,911
What? I'm no longer at 100%?

182
00:08:56,995 --> 00:08:57,996
[MAGNA] This is just half of it?

183
00:08:58,079 --> 00:08:59,038
[gasps]

184
00:08:59,414 --> 00:09:01,416
[MAGNA] That's an insane
amount of power, man.

185
00:09:01,499 --> 00:09:02,792
No way a peasant like me

186
00:09:02,876 --> 00:09:04,919
could ever throw around
that kind of magic.

187
00:09:05,587 --> 00:09:08,131
Which is why
I came up with this spell.

188
00:09:08,757 --> 00:09:09,758
[grunting]

189
00:09:11,092 --> 00:09:13,678
-Secret Flame Magic...
-[gasps]

190
00:09:13,762 --> 00:09:16,222
...Soul Chain Death Match!

191
00:09:16,890 --> 00:09:19,684
[DANTE] I didn't even feel
his first attack, but now...

192
00:09:21,144 --> 00:09:22,187
[clangs]

193
00:09:22,270 --> 00:09:24,397
I combined your magic
with my magic

194
00:09:24,481 --> 00:09:25,940
and then split 'em up evenly.

195
00:09:26,024 --> 00:09:28,568
Figured the only way
to fight you ultimate bastards

196
00:09:28,651 --> 00:09:30,987
-was to level the playing field.
-[clinks]

197
00:09:31,780 --> 00:09:33,656
Now, how about
I introduce myself?

198
00:09:33,740 --> 00:09:34,699
[grunts]

199
00:09:34,783 --> 00:09:36,409
I'm Magna Swing,

200
00:09:36,493 --> 00:09:39,120
a Magic Knight
with the Black Bulls!

201
00:09:39,204 --> 00:09:41,956
And I'm the peasant
who's gonna kick your ass!

202
00:09:42,832 --> 00:09:44,125
-[thuds]
-[grunts]

203
00:09:44,876 --> 00:09:46,085
Please, Zora,

204
00:09:46,169 --> 00:09:48,087
I need you to teach me
to fight like you do.

205
00:09:49,798 --> 00:09:50,965
When I went to train in
the Heart Kingdom, they told me

206
00:09:51,341 --> 00:09:54,385
I couldn't use the Mana Method
because my mana was so low.

207
00:09:55,220 --> 00:09:57,847
But from what I saw,
it seemed like you managed it,

208
00:09:57,931 --> 00:10:00,099
even though
you're a peasant like me.

209
00:10:00,183 --> 00:10:01,226
The spell that doubles stuff

210
00:10:01,309 --> 00:10:03,019
and knocks it back
is super cool.

211
00:10:03,728 --> 00:10:05,730
And you can do it
even without tons of mana.

212
00:10:05,814 --> 00:10:06,940
Please,

213
00:10:07,273 --> 00:10:09,609
that jerk Luck is just gonna
keep getting stronger.

214
00:10:09,692 --> 00:10:12,487
I can't sit here doing nothing
while he pulls ahead of me.

215
00:10:12,570 --> 00:10:13,613
I can't!

216
00:10:13,696 --> 00:10:14,781
-[thuds]
-[grunts]

217
00:10:14,864 --> 00:10:15,990
And the squad,

218
00:10:16,074 --> 00:10:17,575
the last thing
they need right now

219
00:10:17,659 --> 00:10:19,536
is someone weak
holding them back.

220
00:10:21,412 --> 00:10:23,206
[ZORA]
A peasant with flame magic

221
00:10:23,289 --> 00:10:25,542
who made it
into the Magic Knights.

222
00:10:26,209 --> 00:10:28,586
I've got no interest
in seeing you grovel.

223
00:10:28,670 --> 00:10:30,839
I'll teach you,
so get up already.

224
00:10:30,922 --> 00:10:32,298
For real?

225
00:10:33,007 --> 00:10:36,177
-Follow me.
-[effort grunting] Hell yeah!

226
00:10:36,261 --> 00:10:38,054
[ZORA] We might figure out
more new stuff

227
00:10:38,138 --> 00:10:39,806
with two of us anyway.

228
00:10:39,889 --> 00:10:41,891
♪

229
00:10:42,642 --> 00:10:44,310
[papers rustling]

230
00:10:47,939 --> 00:10:48,815
What's this?

231
00:10:49,858 --> 00:10:51,192
[Zora snickers]

232
00:10:51,276 --> 00:10:53,236
Welcome to my secret base.

233
00:10:53,903 --> 00:10:55,947
I've been looking
for the same thing you are.

234
00:10:56,573 --> 00:10:58,199
The best version of myself.

235
00:10:58,908 --> 00:11:00,869
What you said before was right

236
00:11:00,952 --> 00:11:03,788
about using that Mana Method
thing for my spells.

237
00:11:04,539 --> 00:11:06,374
From what I heard,
in the Heart Kingdom,

238
00:11:06,457 --> 00:11:08,710
they put together
the Mana Method on the spot,

239
00:11:08,793 --> 00:11:10,587
tailoring it
to their current fight.

240
00:11:11,170 --> 00:11:12,213
To use that style,

241
00:11:12,297 --> 00:11:14,507
you need a ton of magic,
good instinct,

242
00:11:14,591 --> 00:11:15,925
-and quick reflexes.
-[exclaims]

243
00:11:16,593 --> 00:11:18,970
'Course, as a peasant,
I don't have any of that,

244
00:11:19,053 --> 00:11:20,513
so I gotta spend a lot of time

245
00:11:20,597 --> 00:11:22,390
putting the rune arrays
together.

246
00:11:22,473 --> 00:11:23,516
That's even more true

247
00:11:23,892 --> 00:11:26,186
for powerful ones
like that counter-trap spell.

248
00:11:27,020 --> 00:11:29,814
Fortunately,
peasants have an advantage, too.

249
00:11:30,481 --> 00:11:33,318
Runes created with our puny mana
are so puny

250
00:11:33,401 --> 00:11:36,029
that they just stick around
instead of dispersing.

251
00:11:37,197 --> 00:11:39,657
Which means
we can take all the time we need

252
00:11:39,741 --> 00:11:42,035
and build super complicated
arrays in advance.

253
00:11:42,702 --> 00:11:43,953
Nice, right?

254
00:11:44,037 --> 00:11:45,455
But to make it work,
we have to know

255
00:11:45,538 --> 00:11:47,707
more about mana
and about ourselves.

256
00:11:48,625 --> 00:11:50,251
It's a lot of studying,

257
00:11:50,335 --> 00:11:52,712
a bunch of slow,
boring, difficult work.

258
00:11:53,755 --> 00:11:55,131
[chuckles]

259
00:11:55,215 --> 00:11:56,758
You're stupid
and short-tempered,

260
00:11:56,841 --> 00:11:58,635
so we'll see how this goes.

261
00:11:59,552 --> 00:12:01,095
[MAGNA]
I've always used my magic

262
00:12:01,179 --> 00:12:02,805
without thinking too much
about it.

263
00:12:03,598 --> 00:12:04,891
But the more I learn about mana,

264
00:12:04,974 --> 00:12:07,268
the more I realize
there is to know.

265
00:12:08,394 --> 00:12:10,772
I can't just do
whatever Zora does.

266
00:12:10,855 --> 00:12:13,524
I need something that'll work
well with my attribute

267
00:12:13,608 --> 00:12:14,734
and help me beat a guy

268
00:12:14,817 --> 00:12:17,111
with an insane amount
of magic power.

269
00:12:17,195 --> 00:12:18,738
[groaning]

270
00:12:18,821 --> 00:12:21,115
[screams in frustration]
I'd win on sheer grit

271
00:12:21,199 --> 00:12:24,035
if my magic was anywhere close
to as strong as his!

272
00:12:25,161 --> 00:12:27,455
Uh? Hey, bro-- [frantic yelping]

273
00:12:27,538 --> 00:12:29,248
-Listen!
-Since when am I your "bro"?

274
00:12:29,332 --> 00:12:31,918
I've got an idea for an array.
Check it.

275
00:12:34,587 --> 00:12:36,839
[ZORA]
This never even occurred to me,

276
00:12:36,923 --> 00:12:38,258
but it might just work.

277
00:12:38,883 --> 00:12:41,844
-You could be onto something.
-[chuckles]

278
00:12:42,720 --> 00:12:44,722
[ZORA] It'll probably take
a hell of a lot of time

279
00:12:44,806 --> 00:12:46,516
and patience to make, though.

280
00:12:46,599 --> 00:12:47,767
♪

281
00:12:56,401 --> 00:12:58,361
-[strained grunting]
-[light scraping]

282
00:12:59,779 --> 00:13:02,657
[MAGNA] I spent six months
constructing this spell.

283
00:13:02,740 --> 00:13:06,411
A spell that's mine alone
and that I can only use once.

284
00:13:06,494 --> 00:13:10,665
Secret Flame Magic:
Soul Chain Death Match.

285
00:13:10,748 --> 00:13:11,958
-[grunts]
-[MAGNA] I mean,

286
00:13:12,041 --> 00:13:13,710
it's not that complicated,
really.

287
00:13:14,377 --> 00:13:16,921
I just linked us up
and split our magic in half.

288
00:13:17,005 --> 00:13:19,215
Makes for a fair fight,
don't you think?

289
00:13:19,882 --> 00:13:21,467
Oh, and speaking of fairness,

290
00:13:21,551 --> 00:13:22,969
I guess I ought to warn ya,

291
00:13:23,052 --> 00:13:25,722
-that chain is our souls.
-[flames roaring]

292
00:13:25,805 --> 00:13:28,224
Yank it out or destroy it
and you'll lose your mind.

293
00:13:28,308 --> 00:13:30,435
So you might wanna be careful,
all right?

294
00:13:30,518 --> 00:13:31,519
-Let's go.
-[chain rattling]

295
00:13:32,228 --> 00:13:33,146
[JACK] No way!

296
00:13:33,438 --> 00:13:35,898
A peasant
pulled off a spell like that?

297
00:13:35,982 --> 00:13:38,234
[ZORA] Took a lot of work,
but, yeah, he did.

298
00:13:38,317 --> 00:13:40,028
If we go charging in to help,

299
00:13:40,111 --> 00:13:42,280
we could mess
with the spell's effectiveness,

300
00:13:42,363 --> 00:13:44,532
so we'll need to hang back here.

301
00:13:44,615 --> 00:13:46,200
You had your turn.

302
00:13:46,284 --> 00:13:48,161
Now it's his fight.

303
00:13:50,663 --> 00:13:51,622
[retching]

304
00:13:52,332 --> 00:13:53,541
Gravity Magic:

305
00:13:53,624 --> 00:13:55,084
Heavy Infighting!

306
00:13:55,168 --> 00:13:56,919
-[loud crash]
-[energy crackling]

307
00:13:57,003 --> 00:13:59,464
[glass shattering]

308
00:14:00,381 --> 00:14:02,091
You gave
that little speech before

309
00:14:02,175 --> 00:14:04,343
about attacking
to my heart's content.

310
00:14:04,427 --> 00:14:05,803
Change your mind?

311
00:14:05,887 --> 00:14:07,388
You thief.

312
00:14:07,472 --> 00:14:09,682
Shut up and die!

313
00:14:09,766 --> 00:14:10,767
[Magna grunts]

314
00:14:11,309 --> 00:14:14,062
[DANTE] Gravity Magic:
Presence of the Demon King!

315
00:14:15,021 --> 00:14:17,982
Remember, we've got
the same amount of magic power.

316
00:14:18,733 --> 00:14:21,069
I can take
whatever you dish out!

317
00:14:23,738 --> 00:14:24,906
[grunts]

318
00:14:24,989 --> 00:14:26,949
[chuckling maliciously]

319
00:14:30,119 --> 00:14:31,079
[thwacks]

320
00:14:31,162 --> 00:14:32,080
Keep trying.

321
00:14:34,624 --> 00:14:35,958
But it won't work.

322
00:14:36,959 --> 00:14:38,836
No matter how seriously
you injure me,

323
00:14:38,920 --> 00:14:40,630
my magic will just
repair the damage.

324
00:14:41,214 --> 00:14:42,423
[grunts]

325
00:14:42,882 --> 00:14:45,468
Even with that little trick
of yours, you'll never beat me,

326
00:14:45,551 --> 00:14:46,677
peasant!

327
00:14:46,761 --> 00:14:48,679
-[grunts]
-Get on your knees...

328
00:14:49,514 --> 00:14:51,474
in the dirt where you belong,

329
00:14:52,183 --> 00:14:53,267
and repent...

330
00:14:53,976 --> 00:14:55,311
your defiance!

331
00:14:58,272 --> 00:15:00,817
[ZORA] However many times
life knocked you down,

332
00:15:00,900 --> 00:15:03,069
you got back up
and continued to fight.

333
00:15:03,152 --> 00:15:06,906
You kept your fire burning
for when you'd need it most.

334
00:15:08,449 --> 00:15:11,077
It doesn't matter
if he's the enemy's leader,

335
00:15:11,160 --> 00:15:12,745
a devil host,

336
00:15:12,829 --> 00:15:14,288
or immortal.

337
00:15:16,082 --> 00:15:17,166
-Win this...
-Huh?

338
00:15:17,250 --> 00:15:19,460
[Magna yelling]

339
00:15:19,544 --> 00:15:20,586
...Magna!

340
00:15:25,508 --> 00:15:26,717
-[electricity crackling]
-[grunts]

341
00:15:26,801 --> 00:15:28,219
I know this magic.

342
00:15:30,513 --> 00:15:32,140
-[sizzling]
-[chain rattling]

343
00:15:32,849 --> 00:15:34,851
[DANTE] How dare you, maggot.

344
00:15:34,934 --> 00:15:36,936
Punching me in the face?

345
00:15:37,019 --> 00:15:39,730
Knocking me to the ground
where you should be?

346
00:15:41,983 --> 00:15:43,776
[grunting angrily]

347
00:15:53,327 --> 00:15:54,620
[grunts]

348
00:15:56,706 --> 00:15:58,457
[Magna yelling]

349
00:16:01,002 --> 00:16:04,422
[DANTE] You stole half my magic
with your underhanded spell.

350
00:16:04,964 --> 00:16:07,508
But even if we both attack
with the same strength,

351
00:16:07,592 --> 00:16:09,844
you'll continue taking damage

352
00:16:09,927 --> 00:16:11,888
while I continue to regenerate.

353
00:16:13,055 --> 00:16:16,184
You started too far behind me
to ever catch up!

354
00:16:16,267 --> 00:16:17,894
You are not the one!

355
00:16:18,561 --> 00:16:21,147
You are a grotesque,
embarrassing little creature,

356
00:16:21,230 --> 00:16:24,484
not the kind of opponent
who can bring me true joy!

357
00:16:27,361 --> 00:16:28,404
[MAGNA] What was I thinking?

358
00:16:30,531 --> 00:16:32,366
I'm nothing but a peasant.

359
00:16:33,409 --> 00:16:36,537
I wasn't born powerful
like a noble or a royal.

360
00:16:37,705 --> 00:16:39,040
I'm not Luck,

361
00:16:39,123 --> 00:16:41,626
who has amazing instincts
even if he is a commoner.

362
00:16:42,210 --> 00:16:44,629
And I'm not Asta,
who's a peasant too,

363
00:16:44,712 --> 00:16:47,089
but has something incredible
like anti-magic.

364
00:16:49,967 --> 00:16:52,094
I'm just... me.

365
00:16:52,720 --> 00:16:54,263
[YAMI] Did you have fun
in the Heart Kingdom?

366
00:16:54,347 --> 00:16:55,264
[grunts]

367
00:16:56,515 --> 00:16:58,309
[MAGNA] Uh, uh, [stammers] yeah,

368
00:16:58,392 --> 00:17:00,978
but li-listen,
c-can I ask you something?

369
00:17:01,062 --> 00:17:02,063
[YAMI] What's up?

370
00:17:02,688 --> 00:17:04,065
I was just wondering

371
00:17:04,148 --> 00:17:06,067
why you let me join your squad.

372
00:17:06,150 --> 00:17:07,818
-Why? Hmm.
-[paper rustling]

373
00:17:08,903 --> 00:17:11,364
Maybe 'cause I thought
we'd have similar interests.

374
00:17:12,198 --> 00:17:13,991
-Oh, okay.
-[puffs]

375
00:17:14,784 --> 00:17:15,910
-And also...
-Uh?

376
00:17:16,494 --> 00:17:17,411
[grunts]

377
00:17:18,955 --> 00:17:20,373
...'cause when it came to guts,

378
00:17:20,456 --> 00:17:21,916
you had more of 'em than anyone.

379
00:17:22,917 --> 00:17:24,669
[exclaims]

380
00:17:26,337 --> 00:17:27,505
-[clinks]
-[MAGNA] Yeah.

381
00:17:27,588 --> 00:17:29,465
♪

382
00:17:30,466 --> 00:17:31,634
That's right!

383
00:17:33,344 --> 00:17:37,265
If it comes down to guts,
no one can beat me!

384
00:17:37,348 --> 00:17:40,017
[both grunting]

385
00:17:41,936 --> 00:17:44,188
[Magna yelling]

386
00:17:51,028 --> 00:17:54,115
[yelling]

387
00:18:03,332 --> 00:18:05,793
[MAGNA] I busted my brain
coming up with this spell

388
00:18:05,876 --> 00:18:07,920
and busted my ass
getting it to work,

389
00:18:08,838 --> 00:18:10,923
And now, you're gonna
complain about it?

390
00:18:11,007 --> 00:18:13,342
Like hell, you jackass!

391
00:18:13,968 --> 00:18:16,095
[yelling]

392
00:18:16,971 --> 00:18:19,515
-[Dante laughs maniacally]
-[chain rattling]

393
00:18:20,433 --> 00:18:21,934
[grunts]

394
00:18:24,145 --> 00:18:27,148
[both grunting]

395
00:18:34,238 --> 00:18:36,991
-[Magna yelling]
-[Dante laughs maniacally]

396
00:18:38,784 --> 00:18:39,869
[groans]

397
00:18:42,163 --> 00:18:46,125
[yelling]

398
00:18:46,208 --> 00:18:47,501
-[grunts]
-[groans]

399
00:18:47,585 --> 00:18:49,337
[both continue grunting]

400
00:18:54,508 --> 00:18:56,719
[MAGNA] I'm gonna knock you
to the ground again,

401
00:18:56,802 --> 00:18:59,847
and this time,
you won't be getting back up!

402
00:19:05,478 --> 00:19:06,979
[Dante chuckles]

403
00:19:07,063 --> 00:19:08,397
Nice attempt.

404
00:19:09,231 --> 00:19:10,691
Do you understand now?

405
00:19:11,317 --> 00:19:14,862
This is reality,
unfair and unequal.

406
00:19:14,945 --> 00:19:18,074
Those who are inferior
will forever remain so.

407
00:19:18,741 --> 00:19:23,204
All of your struggles
are meaningless!

408
00:19:23,954 --> 00:19:25,081
[grunts]

409
00:19:28,626 --> 00:19:30,419
Huh? What the--

410
00:19:31,045 --> 00:19:32,922
My devil powers disappeared?

411
00:19:33,422 --> 00:19:35,633
No, impossible.

412
00:19:36,342 --> 00:19:38,844
More tricks?
What the hell did you do now?

413
00:19:38,928 --> 00:19:41,097
[chuckles, coughs]

414
00:19:41,180 --> 00:19:43,557
I didn't do a damn thing,
you moron.

415
00:19:44,183 --> 00:19:45,434
No spells or tricks.

416
00:19:45,518 --> 00:19:48,145
You and I are just out of mana,
that's all.

417
00:19:48,229 --> 00:19:49,146
[gasps]

418
00:19:49,605 --> 00:19:51,690
Wouldn't know how that feels,
though, would ya?

419
00:19:51,774 --> 00:19:55,236
A monster like you has probably
never run out before.

420
00:19:55,319 --> 00:19:56,946
You're not used to
going up against someone

421
00:19:57,029 --> 00:19:58,781
who's as strong as you either.

422
00:19:58,864 --> 00:20:00,991
Otherwise, you might have
realized that holding me off

423
00:20:01,075 --> 00:20:04,078
was burning through
a shit-ton of your mana.

424
00:20:05,204 --> 00:20:07,373
[DANTE] I've lost
my connection to Lucifero

425
00:20:07,456 --> 00:20:09,834
and the abilities it granted me.

426
00:20:10,584 --> 00:20:12,211
My gravity magic,

427
00:20:12,294 --> 00:20:14,588
my super-regenerative
body magic.

428
00:20:14,672 --> 00:20:18,551
[MAGNA] Now you can't use any
spells that are worth a damn.

429
00:20:18,634 --> 00:20:21,470
-Well, the same goes for you--
-[grunting]

430
00:20:22,555 --> 00:20:23,806
[impact grunts]

431
00:20:23,889 --> 00:20:25,474
[blood squelching]

432
00:20:25,558 --> 00:20:27,977
[grunts, exclaims in horror]

433
00:20:29,520 --> 00:20:31,480
[groaning]

434
00:20:31,564 --> 00:20:33,357
♪

435
00:20:33,441 --> 00:20:34,942
[inhales deeply]

436
00:20:35,025 --> 00:20:37,111
There's no way I can lose.

437
00:20:37,194 --> 00:20:38,487
It's not possible!

438
00:20:38,571 --> 00:20:40,573
You can't defeat me!

439
00:20:42,032 --> 00:20:44,869
You are nobody!

440
00:20:47,371 --> 00:20:48,998
Pulverize him!

441
00:20:51,792 --> 00:20:52,960
[grins]

442
00:20:53,878 --> 00:20:58,674
[yelling]

443
00:20:59,967 --> 00:21:02,928
I can't lose... to you!

444
00:21:03,012 --> 00:21:04,805
[MAGNA] Shut up!

445
00:21:04,889 --> 00:21:09,101
You damn psycho!

446
00:21:09,185 --> 00:21:10,936
[chain rattling]

447
00:21:11,020 --> 00:21:13,147
[groans, heaves]

448
00:21:15,065 --> 00:21:16,984
-[clinking]
-[wind howling]

449
00:21:22,698 --> 00:21:24,200
-[zaps]
-[Asta grunts]

450
00:21:24,283 --> 00:21:26,202
-[electricity crackling]
-[wind howling]

451
00:21:30,956 --> 00:21:32,249
[exclaims]

452
00:21:35,836 --> 00:21:37,463
[body thuds]

453
00:21:38,839 --> 00:21:41,717
[Magna breathing shakily]

454
00:21:44,678 --> 00:21:51,435
[screaming]

455
00:21:52,812 --> 00:21:54,813
♪

456
00:21:56,815 --> 00:21:58,275
[exclaims happily]

457
00:21:58,359 --> 00:22:00,486
[Jack exclaims in shock]

458
00:22:02,112 --> 00:22:03,239
[exhales weakly]

459
00:22:05,741 --> 00:22:06,617
Huh?

460
00:22:07,284 --> 00:22:10,037
Well, it looks like you won.
Good job.

461
00:22:10,955 --> 00:22:12,414
Looks like it.

462
00:22:12,498 --> 00:22:13,874
Thanks for your help, bro.

463
00:22:14,542 --> 00:22:16,168
Seriously,
enough with the "bro" stuff.

464
00:22:17,586 --> 00:22:18,838
[chuckles weakly]

465
00:22:20,548 --> 00:22:22,591
[♪ closing theme song playing]

